<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1082" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγχώμᾰλος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁμαλός</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>nearly equal</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγχώμαλοι ἐν χειροτονίᾳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					3.49
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. μάχη</span>
			<i>a doubtful</i> battle, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				4.134
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν νίκην ἐν ἀγχωμάλψ καταλιπόντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>BJ</u>
					6.2.6
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ πλῆθος οὐκ ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Caes.</u>
					42
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				5.14
			</span></i>:—neut. pl. as Adv., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγχώμαλα ναυμαχεῖν</span>, Lat. <i>aequo
				Marte pugnare</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				7.71
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. σφισι ἐγένετο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Herm.</u>
					12
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-άλως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>VH</u>
					2.37
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				App.
				<u>Praef.</u>
				11
			</span></i>.</div>
